tc32: scroll with XCopyArea also when the window is partly covered
(SLOW_REFRESH, the state after VisibilityPartiallyObscured and at
startup), not only when fully visible. Under jwm the rxvt window is
rarely reported Unobscured, so every scroll redrew all text; with
Xfbdev on wd90c24fb a CopyArea is one BITBLT copy. Covered parts come
back as GraphicsExpose, which rxvt already handles.

--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -2086,7 +2086,8 @@
  *    This has been deliberately kept simple.
  */
     i = h->num_scr;
-    if (refresh_type == FAST_REFRESH && h->num_scr_allow && i
+    if ((refresh_type == FAST_REFRESH || refresh_type == SLOW_REFRESH)
+	&& h->num_scr_allow && i
 	&& abs(i) < r->TermWin.nrow && !must_clear) {
 	int16_t         nits;
 	int             j;
